  "question": {
    "text": "Two simple harmonic motions, as shown, are at right angles. They are combined to form Lissajous figures.\n$x(t)=A \\sin (a t+\\delta)$\n$y(t)=B \\sin (b t)$\nIdentify the correct match below",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "b3zTb",
      "text": "\nParameters: $\\mathrm{A}=\\mathrm{B}, \\mathrm{a}=2 \\mathrm{~b} ; \\delta=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$; Curve: Circle\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ijryA",
      "text": "\nParameters: $\\mathrm{A}=\\mathrm{B}, \\mathrm{a}=\\mathrm{b} ; \\delta=\\frac{\\pi}{2} ;$ Curve: Line\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "fsF1C",
      "text": "\nParameters: $\\mathrm{A} \\neq \\mathrm{B}, \\mathrm{a}=\\mathrm{b} ; \\delta=\\frac{\\pi}{2} ;$ Curve: Ellipse\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "WqzU3",
      "text": "\nParameters: $\\mathrm{A} \\neq \\mathrm{B}, \\mathrm{a}=\\mathrm{b} ; \\delta=0$; Curve: Parabola",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "From the two mutually perpendicular S.H.M.'s, the general equation of Lissajous figure,\n$$\n\\frac{x^2}{A^2}+\\frac{y^2}{B^2}-\\frac{2 x y}{A B} \\cos \\delta=\\sin ^2 \\delta\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&x=A \\sin (a t+\\delta) \\\\\n&y=B \\sin (b t+r)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nClearly $A \\neq B$ hence ellipse.",
    "image": null
  },
